# Kitchen Hub cloud lists - copy this file to cloud.conf and fill in your own values.
# Without cloud.conf the shopping list, board and recipes still work on the fridge alone.
#
# 1. gist.github.com -> new SECRET gist, one file named hub.tsv containing:  #hub v1
#    The GIST_ID is the long code at the end of the gist's address.
# 2. github.com -> Settings -> Developer settings -> Fine-grained tokens -> new token,
#    Account permissions -> Gists: Read and write. Longest expiry it offers.
# 3. Make a public repo (e.g. kitchen-hub), upload the 4 files from the phone/ folder,
#    Settings -> Pages -> deploy from branch. That address is PAGES_URL.
# Locks the list text AND your books in the gists so only your phone, the Kindle and your cloud brain can read them.
# The phone learns it from the pairing QR; the cloud brain needs the same value as the HUB_PASS secret.
# Use a long one (four or five unrelated words). Change it on ALL sides if you ever change it.
# Never put your real passphrase in this example file - the repo is public.
PASSPHRASE=change-me-to-four-random-words
GIST_ID=paste_gist_id_here
GH_TOKEN=paste_token_here
PAGES_URL=https://yourname.github.io/kitchen-hub/
# (the repo address github.com/you/repo works too - the hub converts it)

# Optional: your own ntfy channel for timer alerts (otherwise the hub makes a private random one)
# NTFY_TOPIC=kitchenhub-yourname-12345
